text:
Understood, and it simplifies a lot: the face never ASKS. grantFace PUSHES it what it needs, by owner command, whenever grants.json changes. So:
- the 'route?' question (face to owner) goes away, with its RAM cache, the new-name budget and the minute-long 'no such route' memory;
- the face holds a pushed table: name to target key, plus those keys as contacts. Caddy's certificate check reads the same table;
- on your node, 'serve' for your own apps stays: the face forwards to your key, and your node hands it to the app's pipe.
ONE THING IT NEEDS: a way for an owner command to write that table on the face. Today the face carries only 'contact'. The narrowest option is one verb on the face's own appFaceApp, e.g. 'routes.set' reached through the api call, rather than giving the owner the face's whole file system ('fs'). I'd pick the narrow verb.
Go! = the face's table is pushed by grantFace through one narrow verb, and route? is removed.
